                        "status":  "NOT_PROVEN",
                        "response":  "- Do not declare the native method public: make the native method private and expose the functionality through a public Java-based wrapper that performs checks before calling the native method.  \n- Make a defensive copy of mutable input in the wrapper (example: data = data.clone()).  \n- Validate offset and length in a way that avoids integer overflow: ensure offset \u003e= 0, len \u003e= 0, and offset \u003c= data.length - len; if these checks fail, throw an IllegalArgumentException.  \n- Perform all necessary input validation in the wrapper prior to invoking the private native method.",
